# Rust / Anchor build output.
#
# Unlike the old repo, NOTHING under target/ is re-included. The old repo committed
# its program-identity keypair at target/deploy/<program>-keypair.json so every deploy
# reused the same program ID; that keypair then had to be treated as compromised.
# Blotto Cup keeps the program keypair OUTSIDE the repository — see TRANSITION-REPORT.md
# for the path — and pins the program ID in Anchor.toml and declare_id! instead.
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Anchor
.anchor
.surfpool
test-ledger
.validator-ledger*

# Keys — never committed, in any form. The pre-commit hook in .githooks/pre-commit
# additionally rejects any staged file containing a 64-integer array (the Solana
# keypair JSON shape), wherever it lives.
keys/
keys/*.json
*.pem
*keypair*.json
id.json

# Secrets scan output
pre-scan.json
gitleaks.json

# Environment — only .env.example is tracked, and it carries names with no values.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Node
node_modules
.next
dist
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor
.idea
*.swp
*.swo

# Logs
*.log
